(b) the recipient being unavailable at the times attempted;
(c) a natural event, civil disturbance, strike, or governmental restriction;
(d) a delay in customs clearance not attributable to Pacify's documentation.
S8.4 Where a delay exceeds 15 business days beyond the committed date, the customer may cancel the order
for a full refund including all shipping charges, whether or not the consignment has been dispatched.
S8.5 Claims under this section are made to support@pacify.com and are determined within 3 business days.

S12. When to stop troubleshooting
S12.1 Stop and raise a warranty claim where any of the following is true:
(a) the device shows a code marked "Yes" in the warranty column at S9;
(b) a symptom persists after a factory reset under S11;
(c) an external monitor confirms an internal panel fault under S3.1;
(d) the battery is swollen or the device will not sit flat;
(e) you can smell burning, or the casing is deformed;
(f) a storage or memory test reports errors.
S12.2 Raise the claim under POL-WAR-001 S10. Tell us which steps in this guide you have already tried — it
shortens the diagnosis and is not a condition of the claim.
S12.3 If the device is a third-party brand, the claim goes to that manufacturer's service network rather than to
Pacify. See POL-WAR-001 S8. We can confirm your purchase date and point you to the nearest centre.

S2. What is covered
S2.1 This warranty covers defects in materials and workmanship that manifest under normal use, including:
(a) failure of the item to power on or to hold a charge;
(b) failure of an integrated component including display, keyboard, trackpad, speakers, camera, and ports;
(c) failure of internal storage or memory;
(d) display defects meeting the threshold at S6;
(e) battery degradation meeting the threshold at S5;
(f) failure of a supplied power adapter;
(g) manufacturing faults in casing or hinges, excluding cosmetic wear.
S2.2 Cover extends to the repair of the defect, the replacement of the item, or a refund, determined in
accordance with S11.

S3. What is not covered
S3.1 This warranty does not cover:
(a) liquid ingress or corrosion, however caused;
(b) physical damage including cracks, dents, bends, and impact damage;

(c) damage arising from use of a non-approved charger or accessory;
(d) damage arising from unauthorised repair, disassembly, or modification;
(e) cosmetic wear including scratches, scuffs, keycap shine, and fading;
(f) software faults, operating system errors, driver conflicts, malware, and data loss;
(g) consumable components including styli tips and ear tips;
(h) failure caused by voltage irregularity, lightning, flood, fire, or other external event;
(i) items whose serial number has been removed, altered, or defaced;
(j) normal battery capacity loss not meeting the threshold at S5;
(k) issues arising from third-party software installed by the customer.
S3.2 Where a defect is found on inspection to fall within S3.1, the customer is notified and offered a paid repair
quotation. Inspection in such cases attracts a fee of Rs 750, waived if the paid repair proceeds.

S10. Making a claim
S10.1 Claims are raised through the customer's Pacify account, or by written request to support@pacify.com
quoting the order reference.
S10.2 The following are required:
(a) the order reference and item serial number;
(b) a description of the fault and the date it was first observed;
(c) any error code displayed;
(d) photographs or a short video demonstrating the fault, where the fault is observable;
(e) for battery claims, a capacity reading obtained under S5.2.
S10.3 Where troubleshooting steps in the Technical Support FAQ have been attempted, the customer should
say which. This shortens diagnosis and is not a precondition of the claim.
S10.4 A claim is acknowledged within 1 business day and an inspection outcome is issued within 3 business
days of receipt of the item.

S13.1 Warranty cover is void where:
(a) the item has been opened, disassembled, or repaired by a person not authorised by Pacify or by the
manufacturer;
(b) the serial number has been removed, altered, or rendered illegible;
(c) a security seal internal to the item has been broken;
(d) the item has been used in a commercial rental, mining, or continuous-load application not contemplated by
its specification.
S13.2 The installation of software, including a different operating system, does not void hardware warranty
cover. Faults arising from such software are excluded under S3.1(f) but the hardware remains covered.
